  "comment": "`requirementEdgeLabelBackground` is a theme variable for edge label backgrounds and is semantically unrelated to whether `nodeStyles` should be applied to node paths. Using it as a guard here means: if a theme defines `requirementEdgeLabelBackground` but has no `borderColorArray`, node path styles are still applied; if a theme defines neither, node path styles are silently skipped even when `nodeStyles` is non-empty (e.g. from a user `style` statement). A cleaner condition that expresses the actual intent would be:\n\n```ts\nif (nodeStyles && node.look !== 'handDrawn') {\n  shapeSvg.selectAll('.outer-path path').attr('style', nodeStyles);\n}\n```",
